# Baked terrain mesh chunks are raw little-endian binary (see
# tools/geo_bake/vector_mesh_format.py). Git's heuristic already classifies
# them as binary because the header's reserved field is always zero, but
# stating it means a chunk that happened to contain no NUL byte could never
# be line-ending-converted into corrupt geometry on a checkout.
*.tmesh binary

*.import -text

# Baked per-hex 1890s population capacity, raw little-endian binary (see
# tools/geo_bake/bake_population.py and ZombiePopulationData.gd). Same reason
# as *.tmesh above: its reserved fields are zero so git already reads it as
# binary, but stating it means a file that happened to contain no NUL byte
# could never be line-ending-converted into wrong population numbers.
*.zpop binary
